{
  "analysis": "I see Doom uses myargc/myargv and many libc functions. The previous grep for libc usage didn't show due to truncation. I need to gather the full list of external libc symbols needed, then write a libc shim. doomgeneric_img.c's main calls doomgeneric_Create(argc, argv) with argc=0, which may cause issues in argument parsing. I should modify main to provide a minimal argv with the program name and WAD path.",
  "plan": "Collect undefined symbols after a freestanding compile attempt to see exactly which libc functions are needed. Inspect doomgeneric_Create and related startup to understand argv requirements. Then create a libc shim and adjust main/argv handling.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -n \"doomgeneric_Create\" doomgeneric.c doomgeneric.h doomgeneric_img.c | head -20\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '1,120p' doomgeneric.c\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -n \"doomgeneric_Create\\|dg_ScreenBuffer\\|DG_ScreenBuffer\\|DOOMGENERIC_RESX\\|DOOMGENERIC_RESY\" doomgeneric.h doomgeneric.c doomgeneric_img.c | head -40\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "mipsel-linux-gnu-gcc-12 -nostdlib -ffreestanding -static -march=mips1 -mfp32 -mno-mips16 -mno-interlink-mips16 -O1 -fno-asynchronous-unwind-tables -fno-unwind-tables -fPIC -fno-pic -ffunction-sections -fdata-sections -I. -c *.c -o /dev/null 2>&1 | head -80\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    }
  ]
}
